    "c4": {
      "anchor": "code#list-1",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "Code in a space",
      "excerpt": "A record is JSON-shaped, and text is ordinary JSON, so source fits as it is. Any",
      "text": "Messing with a long spell file is a nightmare.  The record should be the description of the file, then the file itself is a blob that can be edited directly.",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-01T20:10:59.081Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "A record is JSON-shaped, and text is ordinary JSON, so source fits as it is.",
      "offset": 0,
      "edited": "2026-11-01T20:11:34.722Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-01T20:16:39.132Z",
          "html": "<p>Changed: a file is a blob, and its record is just the description. The catch is that how to upload a blob into a Space isn't clear yet, so that's now the first thing the trial tests.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-01T20:16:17.816Z"
      }
    },
    "c5": {
      "anchor": "code#list-1",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "10. Code in a space",
      "excerpt": "A record is JSON-shaped, and text is ordinary JSON, so source fits as it is. Any",
      "text": "files need to have file names, and should be replacable.  e.g. if I'm editing a spell file, it may be saved 1000 times -- we don't want to have 1000 versions of the code sitting in the repo.\n\nBuild this into the proposal, that git is used for all versioning.  Assume that only spell is committing to git, so we don't have to worry about conflicts.",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-01T20:11:48.838Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "which a record points to by its hash",
      "offset": 151,
      "edited": "2026-11-01T20:15:16.262Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-01T20:16:40.233Z",
          "html": "<p>Built in: a file has a name and is replaced in place, so 1,000 saves leave one file, and git holds the versions, with only Spell committing.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-01T20:16:18.858Z"
      }
    },
    "c6": {
      "anchor": "code#list-3",
      "kind": "list",
      "label": "10. Code in a space",
      "excerpt": "A record can be at most 1 MiB, which is plenty for a source file, but not for a",
      "text": "versions of files are managed by git, each file in the space is the \"current\" version of the file, and we can use git history to \"go back.\"\n\nException, when I'm actively editing a file, changes are auto-saved as a single draft.  When I \"stop editing\", I apply the draft which updates the \"real record.\"",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-01T20:13:04.606Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "A Space keeps no history, as its log of changes isn't guaranteed, so Spell has to save versions itself, as records.",
      "offset": 94,
      "edited": "2026-11-01T20:14:22.580Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-01T20:16:41.316Z",
          "html": "<p>Built in, with the one draft you describe. A draft is readable by everyone on its Space's list, so a public page's draft sits in the private space. Git also holds private files, so it's the one place Spell does guard a read.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-01T20:16:20.167Z"
      }
    },
    "c7": {
